# Keep secrets and bulk data out of the image.
#
# THE FIRST BLOCK IS THE IMPORTANT ONE. `COPY . .` copies whatever is in the
# build context, including an untracked .env sitting next to the Dockerfile. A
# credential in an image layer survives every later layer that deletes it, and
# the image is pushed to a registry.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# Bulk data. data/** is gitignored anyway, but a local checkout has gigabytes of
# panels and box scores in it and every byte would be sent to the builder.
data/
outputs/
*.parquet
*.xlsx
*.sqlite

# Build and tooling noise. catboost_info/ is a training log CatBoost drops in
# the working directory, and *.zip catches a training pack or an export sitting
# in the checkout; both are gitignored, and neither belongs in an image layer.
catboost_info/
*.zip
*.pdf
.git/
.github/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
htmlcov/
.coverage
node_modules/
